{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Slaughter a slaughter.</b> He gave this command to Menasheh his son, for the sons of Jacob were scrupulous regarding ritual slaughter." "<b>And prepare.</b> This refers to the fat. <br>Or one may interpret <b>והכן</b> — 'and prepare' — as that he scheduled them for the eve of Sabbath for the Sabbath day, in the manner of what is written (Exodus 16:5): ״והיה ביום הששי והכינו״ and so forth. And so you find in Bereshit Rabbah: <b>והכן</b> — there is no 'והכן' but the Sabbath, as it is said ״והכינו את אשר יביאו״ — this teaches that Joseph observed the Sabbath." "<b>At noon.</b> This is the mealtime of princes and judges who have the affairs of the public to attend to. And thus Scripture disparages those who eat in the morning — that is what Solomon, peace be upon him, said (Ecclesiastes 10:16): ״אי לך ארץ שמלכך נער ושריך בבקר יאכלו״. And he praises those who eat at noon — that is what he said (ibid.): ״אשריך ארץ שמלכך בן חורים ושריך בעת יאכלו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {1 "The phrase 'זה נקור החלב' (this is called the fat) is obscure; rendered hyper-literally; meaning uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:04.727944142Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}